 "text": "..title\nA resolution to amend Ordinance No. BL2023-1796, as amended, to authorize The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to increase the funding for the acquisition of properties for the Dry Creek WRF Flood Mitigation System Project, (MWS Project No. 21-SC-0226).\n..body\nWHEREAS, Ordinance No. BL2023-1796, approved, May 8, 2023, and amended by Resolution No. RS2025-1709, approved December 17, 2025, authorized the acquisition of a portion of three properties and easements through negotiation, condemnation or fee simple take, for three properties located at 1213, 1217 and 1221 Northgate Business Parkway; and,\nWHEREAS, Resolution No. RS2025-1709 did not increase the not to exceed amount of $500,000.00 to account for the additional property cost; and,\nWHEREAS, an increase of $250,000.00 in the not to exceed amount for a total not to exceed amount of $750,000.00, is needed to complete the acquisition of property and easements to construct the Dry Creek WRF Flood Mitigation System project number 21-SC-0226; and,\nWHEREAS, the additional monies are available in Fund No. 47410; and,\nWHEREAS, Ordinance No. BL2023-1796 provides that amendments to the legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThat Ordinance No. BL2023-1796, as amended by Resolution No. RS2025-1709, is hereby amended by increasing the approved funding amount from not to exceed $500,000.00 to not to exceed $750,000.00.\nSection 2. This resolution shall take effect upon passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis resolution amends Ordinance No. BL2023-1796, as amended, to allow the Metropolitan Government to increase the funding for the acquisition of properties for the Dry Creek WRF Flood Mitigation System Project.\n\nOrdinance No. BL2023-1796 authorized the Director of Public Property Administration to acquire a portion of properties located at 1213 and 1217 Northgate Business Parkway. The ordinance capped the amount of funding for these acquisitions at an amount not to exceed $500,000.\n\nThe ordinance was amended by Resolution No. RS2025-1709, which authorized the Director of Public Property to acquire a portion of three properties at 1213, 1217, and 1221 Northgate Business Parkway. \n\nThe proposed resolution would increase approved funding amount for these acquisitions from not to exceed $500,000.00 to not to exceed $750,000.00.\n\nFiscal Note: This amendment increases the funding to acquire three properties for the Dry Creek WRF Flood Mitigation System Project from $500,000 to an amount not to exceed $750,000.\n"
